   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking how someone is",
     "texto": [
      "Hvordan går det? is the everyday way to say «How's it going?». Literally it is close to «how does it go?», but it is not translated word for word.",
      "You can answer Det går bra («It's going well») or Det går fint («It's going fine / very well»). To ask back: Og med deg? («And you?»).",
      "In a normal sentence, ikke comes after the verb, just like English «not» in «it is not»: Det går ikke bra («It is not going well»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
